  "findings": [
    "The normalized target names the Law bachelor specialisation in Business Law, rather than the generic Law target. The current September-2026 programme and adopted Appendix 1e identify the Dutch-taught full-time LLB, overriding the recruitment table’s BSc abbreviation. The first year has ten compulsory six-credit legal foundations. The next two years each total sixty compulsory credits. The final year has eight six-credit courses, four-credit enterprise taxation and an eight-credit thesis. No minor/exchange space is invented from general recruitment remarks.",
    "Article 42 requires ninety degree EC at moot-court registration and ninety at the start of thesis teaching. The dated moot-court entry repeats that later December credits cannot count back to registration; mandatory lectures, court visit, procedural-document workshop, pleading training and oral court presentation are verified. The thesis begins in autumn, spans a full academic year and does not allow normal spring entry. Completing both earlier years meets the thresholds. Article 42’s legacy six-credit thesis code is reconciled with the explicit eight-credit component in Article 44, the dated eight-credit course and the programme table; it does not reduce or add credits.",
    "Non-credit Dutch language testing and Talent and Career Development (OR) are retained outside the 180 EC. The general Law route’s separate Skills Lab thesis prerequisite is not imported into this specialisation: its Article 44 and thesis entry establish the actual applicable conditions. First-year constitutional law precedes the administrative introduction; first-year private, criminal, procedural and company-law study precedes dependent advanced subjects. EU Law requires the first-year international/EU introduction. Both earlier years are completed before the advanced practice and research year.",
    "All thirty dated entries were retrieved. Unchanged shared course research from CP228 is reused only when the actual current JSON agrees, and newly specialisation-specific material was read directly. Introduction to Business Law concerns formation, organisation and termination of corporations/partnerships. Business Law deepens company lifecycles, groups, reorganisations, investor/creditor protection and takeovers. These are not claimed from UCR’s transnational transaction course.",
    "Law/Economics uses incentives, transaction costs, property, liability and strategic interactions in corporate legal questions. Organisation/Strategy uses economic organisation theories, agency, transactions, behavioural theory and competitive advantage. Corporate Finance integrates accounting, equity/debt, valuation, shareholder litigation and entrepreneurial finance. Enterprise Ethics combines normative theories with corporate groups, stakeholders, litigation, human rights and sustainability. Enterprise Taxation covers income/corporate/VAT/transfer/gift/inheritance taxes and their connections. These actual emphases control course contributions and partial placements.",
    "The independent thesis develops legal research questions, literature review, theoretical/analytical/normative frameworks, appropriate doctrinal/empirical/comparative/historical methods and an individual proposal and thesis. No compulsory UCR research is invented as a substitute. The standard required pathway closes at 180 unique EC without a parent/child double count or mutually exclusive branch."
  ]
